			"\r",
			"| Layer | Tool | Purpose |\r",
			"|-------|------|---------|\r",
			"| Core | Python 3.10+, NumPy | Math, array ops, vectorized effects |\r",
			"| Signal | SciPy | FFT, peak detection (audio modes) |\r",
			"| Imaging | Pillow (PIL) | Font rasterization, frame decoding, image I/O |\r",
			"| Video I/O | ffmpeg (CLI) | Decode input, encode output, mux audio |\r",
			"| Parallel | concurrent.futures | N workers for batch/clip rendering |\r",
			"| TTS | ElevenLabs API (optional) | Generate narration clips |\r",
			"| Optional | OpenCV | Video frame sampling, edge detection |\r",
			"\r",
			"## Pipeline Architecture\r",
			"\r",
			"Every mode follows the same 6-stage pipeline:\r",
			"\r",
			"```\r",
			"INPUT → ANALYZE → SCENE_FN → TONEMAP → SHADE → ENCODE\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"1. **INPUT** — Load/decode source material (video frames, audio samples, images, or nothing)\r",
			"2. **ANALYZE** — Extract per-frame features (audio bands, video luminance/edges, motion vectors)\r",
			"3. **SCENE_FN** — Scene function renders to pixel canvas (`uint8 H,W,3`). Composes multiple character grids via `_render_vf()` + pixel blend modes. See `references/composition.md`\r",
			"4. **TONEMAP** — Percentile-based adaptive brightness normalization. See `references/composition.md` § Adaptive Tonemap\r",
			"5. **SHADE** — Post-processing via `ShaderChain` + `FeedbackBuffer`. See `references/shaders.md`\r",
			"6. **ENCODE** — Pipe raw RGB frames to ffmpeg for H.264/GIF encoding\r",
			"\r",
			"## Creative Direction\r",
			"\r",
			"### Aesthetic Dimensions\r",
			"\r",
