			"### Step 2: Technical Design\r",
			"\r",
			"- **Mode** — which of the 6 modes above\r",
			"- **Resolution** — landscape 1920x1080 (default), portrait 1080x1920, square 1080x1080 @ 24fps\r",
			"- **Hardware detection** — auto-detect cores/RAM, set quality profile. See `references/optimization.md`\r",
			"- **Sections** — map timestamps to scene functions, each with its own effect/palette/color/shader config\r",
			"- **Output format** — MP4 (default), GIF (640x360 @ 15fps), PNG sequence\r",
			"\r",
			"### Step 3: Build the Script\r",
			"\r",
			"Single Python file. Components (with references):\r",
			"\r",
			"1. **Hardware detection + quality profile** — `references/optimization.md`\r",
			"2. **Input loader** — mode-dependent; `references/inputs.md`\r",
			"3. **Feature analyzer** — audio FFT, video luminance, or synthetic\r",
			"4. **Grid + renderer** — multi-density grids with bitmap cache; `references/architecture.md`\r",
			"5. **Character palettes** — multiple per project; `references/architecture.md` § Palettes\r",
			"6. **Color system** — HSV + discrete RGB + harmony generation; `references/architecture.md` § Color\r",
			"7. **Scene functions** — each returns `canvas (uint8 H,W,3)`; `references/scenes.md`\r",
			"8. **Tonemap** — adaptive brightness normalization; `references/composition.md`\r",
			"9. **Shader pipeline** — `ShaderChain` + `FeedbackBuffer`; `references/shaders.md`\r",
			"10. **Scene table + dispatcher** — time → scene function + config; `references/scenes.md`\r",
			"11. **Parallel encoder** — N-worker clip rendering with ffmpeg pipes\r",
			"12. **Main** — orchestrate full pipeline\r",
