			"### Step 4: Quality Verification\r",
			"\r",
			"- **Test frames first**: render single frames at key timestamps before full render\r",
			"- **Brightness check**: `canvas.mean() > 8` for all ASCII content. If dark, lower gamma\r",
			"- **Visual coherence**: do all scenes feel like they belong to the same video?\r",
			"- **Creative vision check**: does the output match the concept from Step 1? If it looks generic, go back\r",
			"\r",
			"## Critical Implementation Notes\r",
			"\r",
			"### Brightness — Use `tonemap()`, Not Linear Multipliers\r",
			"\r",
			"This is the #1 visual issue. ASCII on black is inherently dark. **Never use `canvas * N` multipliers** — they clip highlights. Use adaptive tonemap:\r",
			"\r",
			"```python\r",
			"def tonemap(canvas, gamma=0.75):\r",
			"    f = canvas.astype(np.float32)\r",
			"    lo, hi = np.percentile(f[::4, ::4], [1, 99.5])\r",
			"    if hi - lo < 10: hi = lo + 10\r",
			"    f = np.clip((f - lo) / (hi - lo), 0, 1) ** gamma\r",
			"    return (f * 255).astype(np.uint8)\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Pipeline: `scene_fn() → tonemap() → FeedbackBuffer → ShaderChain → ffmpeg`\r",
			"\r",
			"Per-scene gamma: default 0.75, solarize 0.55, posterize 0.50, bright scenes 0.85. Use `screen` blend (not `overlay`) for dark layers.\r",
