			"### User Questions\r",
			"\r",
			"Use the `clarify` tool to confirm options. Since `clarify` handles one question at a time, ask the most important question first and proceed sequentially. See [references/workflow.md](references/workflow.md) for the full Step 2 question set.\r",
			"\r",
			"**Timeout handling (CRITICAL)**: `clarify` can return `\"The user did not provide a response within the time limit. Use your best judgement to make the choice and proceed.\"` — this is NOT user consent to default everything.\r",
			"\r",
			"- Treat it as a default **for that one question only**. Continue asking the remaining Step 2 questions in sequence; each question is an independent consent point.\r",
			"- **Surface the default to the user visibly** in your next message so they have a chance to correct it: e.g. `\"Style: defaulted to ohmsha preset (clarify timed out). Say the word to switch.\"` — an unreported default is indistinguishable from never having asked.\r",
			"- Do NOT collapse Step 2 into a single \"use all defaults\" pass after one timeout. If the user is genuinely absent, they will be equally absent for all five questions — but they can correct visible defaults when they return, and cannot correct invisible ones.\r",
			"\r",
			"### Step 7: Image Generation\r",
			"\r",
			"Use Hermes' built-in `image_generate` tool for all image rendering. Its schema accepts only `prompt` and `aspect_ratio` (`landscape` | `portrait` | `square`); it **returns a URL**, not a local file. Every generated page or character sheet must therefore be downloaded to the output directory.\r",
			"\r",
			"**Prompt file requirement (hard)**: write each image's full, final prompt to a standalone file under `prompts/` (naming: `NN-{type}-[slug].md`) BEFORE calling `image_generate`. The prompt file is the reproducibility record.\r",
			"\r",
			"**Aspect ratio mapping** — the storyboard's `aspect_ratio` field maps to `image_generate`'s format as follows:\r",
			"\r",
