			"**Download step** — after every `image_generate` call:\r",
			"1. Read the URL from the tool result\r",
			"2. Fetch the image bytes using an **absolute** output path, e.g.\r",
			"   `curl -fsSL \"<url>\" -o /abs/path/to/comic/<slug>/NN-page-<slug>.png`\r",
			"3. Verify the file exists and is non-empty at that exact path before proceeding to the next page\r",
			"\r",
			"**Never rely on shell CWD persistence for `-o` paths.** The terminal tool's persistent-shell CWD can change between batches (session expiry, `TERMINAL_LIFETIME_SECONDS`, a failed `cd` that leaves you in the wrong directory). `curl -o relative/path.png` is a silent footgun: if CWD has drifted, the file lands somewhere else with no error. **Always pass a fully-qualified absolute path to `-o`**, or pass `workdir=<abs path>` to the terminal tool. Incident Apr 2026: pages 06-09 of a 10-page comic landed at the repo root instead of `comic/<slug>/` because batch 3 inherited a stale CWD from batch 2 and `curl -o 06-page-skills.png` wrote to the wrong directory. The agent then spent several turns claiming the files existed where they didn't.\r",
			"\r",
			"**7.1 Character sheet** — generate it (to `characters/characters.png`, aspect `landscape`) when the comic is multi-page with recurring characters. Skip for simple presets (e.g., four-panel minimalist) or single-page comics. The prompt file at `characters/characters.md` must exist before invoking `image_generate`. The rendered PNG is a **human-facing review artifact** (so the user can visually verify character design) and a reference for later regenerations or manual prompt edits — it does **not** drive Step 7.2. Page prompts are already written in Step 5 from the **text descriptions** in `characters/characters.md`; `image_generate` cannot accept images as visual input.\r",
			"\r",
			"**7.2 Pages** — each page's prompt MUST already be at `prompts/NN-{cover|page}-[slug].md` before invoking `image_generate`. Because `image_generate` is prompt-only, character consistency is enforced by **embedding character descriptions (sourced from `characters/characters.md`) inline in every page prompt during Step 5**. The embedding is done uniformly whether or not a PNG sheet is produced in 7.1; the PNG is only a review/regeneration aid.\r",
			"\r",
			"**Backup rule**: existing `prompts/…md` and `…png` files → rename with `-backup-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS` suffix before regenerating.\r",
			"\r",
			"Full step-by-step workflow (analysis, storyboard, review gates, regeneration variants): [references/workflow.md](references/workflow.md).\r",
			"\r",
			"## References\r",
			"\r",
			"**Core Templates**:\r",
			"- [analysis-framework.md](references/analysis-framework.md) - Deep content analysis\r",
			"- [character-template.md](references/character-template.md) - Character definition format\r",
			"- [storyboard-template.md](references/storyboard-template.md) - Storyboard structure\r",
			"- [ohmsha-guide.md](references/ohmsha-guide.md) - Ohmsha manga specifics\r",
			"\r",
			"**Style Definitions**:\r",
			"- `references/art-styles/` - Art styles (ligne-claire, manga, realistic, ink-brush, chalk, minimalist)\r",
			"- `references/tones/` - Tones (neutral, warm, dramatic, romantic, energetic, vintage, action)\r",
			"- `references/presets/` - Presets with special rules (ohmsha, wuxia, shoujo, concept-story, four-panel)\r",
			"- `references/layouts/` - Layouts (standard, cinematic, dense, splash, mixed, webtoon, four-panel)\r",
			"\r",
			"**Workflow**:\r",
			"- [workflow.md](references/workflow.md) - Full workflow details\r",
			"- [auto-selection.md](references/auto-selection.md) - Content signal analysis\r",
			"- [partial-workflows.md](references/partial-workflows.md) - Partial workflow options\r",
			"\r",
			"## Page Modification\r",
			"\r",
			"| Action | Steps |\r",
			"|--------|-------|\r",
			"| **Edit** | **Update prompt file FIRST** → regenerate image → download new PNG |\r",
			"| **Add** | Create prompt at position → generate with character descriptions embedded → renumber subsequent → update storyboard |\r",
			"| **Delete** | Remove files → renumber subsequent → update storyboard |\r",
			"\r",
			"**IMPORTANT**: When updating pages, ALWAYS update the prompt file (`prompts/NN-{cover|page}-[slug].md`) FIRST before regenerating. This ensures changes are documented and reproducible.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Pitfalls\r",
			"\r",
			"- Image generation: 10-30 seconds per page; auto-retry once on failure\r",
			"- **Always download** the URL returned by `image_generate` to a local PNG — downstream tooling (and the user's review) expects files in the output directory, not ephemeral URLs\r",
			"- **Use absolute paths for `curl -o`** — never rely on persistent-shell CWD across batches. Silent footgun: files land in the wrong directory and subsequent `ls` on the intended path shows nothing. See Step 7 \"Download step\".\r",
			"- Use stylized alternatives for sensitive public figures\r",
			"- **Step 2 confirmation required** - do not skip\r",
			"- **Steps 4/6 conditional** - only if user requested in Step 2\r",
			"- **Step 7.1 character sheet** - recommended for multi-page comics, optional for simple presets. The PNG is a review/regeneration aid; page prompts (written in Step 5) use the text descriptions in `characters/characters.md`, not the PNG. `image_generate` does not accept images as visual input\r",
			"- **Strip secrets** — scan source content for API keys, tokens, or credentials before writing any output file",
