			"| \"show me live progress\" | script | `ws_monitor.py --prompt-id <id>` |\r",
			"| \"fetch the error from job X\" | script | `fetch_logs.py <prompt_id>` |\r",
			"| **Direct REST** | | |\r",
			"| \"what's in the queue?\" | REST | `curl http://HOST:8188/queue` (local) or `--host https://cloud.comfy.org` |\r",
			"| \"cancel that\" | REST | `curl -X POST http://HOST:8188/interrupt` |\r",
			"| \"free GPU memory\" | REST | `curl -X POST http://HOST:8188/free` |\r",
			"\r",
			"## Setup & Onboarding\r",
			"\r",
			"When a user asks to set up ComfyUI, **the FIRST thing to do is ask whether\r",
			"they want Comfy Cloud (hosted, zero install, API key) or Local (install\r",
			"ComfyUI on their machine)**. Don't start running install commands or hardware\r",
			"checks until they've answered.\r",
			"\r",
			"**Official docs:** https://docs.comfy.org/installation\r",
			"**CLI docs:** https://docs.comfy.org/comfy-cli/getting-started\r",
			"**Cloud docs:** https://docs.comfy.org/get_started/cloud\r",
			"**Cloud API:** https://docs.comfy.org/development/cloud/overview\r",
			"\r",
			"### Step 0: Ask Local vs Cloud (ALWAYS FIRST)\r",
			"\r",
			"Suggested script:\r",
			"\r",
			"> \"Do you want to run ComfyUI locally on your machine, or use Comfy Cloud?\r",
			">\r",
			"> - **Comfy Cloud** — hosted on RTX 6000 Pro GPUs, all common models pre-installed,\r",
			">   zero setup. Requires an API key (paid subscription required to actually run\r",
			">   workflows; free tier is read-only). Best if you don't have a capable GPU.\r",
			"> - **Local** — free, but your machine MUST meet the hardware requirements:\r",
			">   - NVIDIA GPU with **≥6 GB VRAM** (≥8 GB for SDXL, ≥12 GB for Flux/video), OR\r",
			">   - AMD GPU with ROCm support (Linux), OR\r",
			">   - Apple Silicon Mac (M1+) with **≥16 GB unified memory** (≥32 GB recommended).\r",
			">   - Intel Macs and machines with no GPU will NOT work — use Cloud instead.\r",
			">\r",
			"> Which would you like?\"\r",
			"\r",
			"Routing:\r",
			"\r",
			"- **Cloud** → skip to **Path A**.\r",
			"- **Local** → run hardware check first, then pick a path from Paths B–E based on the verdict.\r",
			"- **Unsure** → run the hardware check and let the verdict decide.\r",
			"\r",
			"### Step 1: Verify Hardware (ONLY if user chose local)\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"python3 scripts/hardware_check.py --json\r",
			"# Optional: also probe `torch` for actual CUDA/MPS:\r",
			"python3 scripts/hardware_check.py --json --check-pytorch\r",
