			"### Run directly from the Hugging Face Hub\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"llama-cli -hf bartowski/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-GGUF:Q8_0\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"llama-server -hf bartowski/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-GGUF:Q8_0\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Run an exact GGUF file from the Hub\r",
			"\r",
			"Use this when the tree API shows custom file naming or the exact HF snippet is missing.\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"llama-server \\\r",
			"    --hf-repo microsoft/Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct-gguf \\\r",
			"    --hf-file Phi-3-mini-4k-instruct-q4.gguf \\\r",
			"    -c 4096\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### OpenAI-compatible server check\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"curl http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\r",
			"    \"messages\": [\r",
			"      {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Write a limerick about Python exceptions\"}\r",
			"    ]\r",
			"  }'\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"## Python bindings (llama-cpp-python)\r",
			"\r",
			"`pip install llama-cpp-python` (CUDA: `CMAKE_ARGS=\"-DGGML_CUDA=on\" pip install llama-cpp-python --force-reinstall --no-cache-dir`; Metal: `CMAKE_ARGS=\"-DGGML_METAL=on\" ...`).\r",
			"\r",
			"### Basic generation\r",
			"\r",
			"```python\r",
			"from llama_cpp import Llama\r",
			"\r",
			"llm = Llama(\r",
			"    model_path=\"./model-q4_k_m.gguf\",\r",
			"    n_ctx=4096,\r",
			"    n_gpu_layers=35,     # 0 for CPU, 99 to offload everything\r",
			"    n_threads=8,\r",
			")\r",
			"\r",
			"out = llm(\"What is machine learning?\", max_tokens=256, temperature=0.7)\r",
			"print(out[\"choices\"][0][\"text\"])\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Chat + streaming\r",
			"\r",
			"```python\r",
			"llm = Llama(\r",
			"    model_path=\"./model-q4_k_m.gguf\",\r",
			"    n_ctx=4096,\r",
			"    n_gpu_layers=35,\r",
			"    chat_format=\"llama-3\",   # or \"chatml\", \"mistral\", etc.\r",
			")\r",
			"\r",
			"resp = llm.create_chat_completion(\r",
			"    messages=[\r",
			"        {\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a helpful assistant.\"},\r",
			"        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What is Python?\"},\r",
			"    ],\r",
			"    max_tokens=256,\r",
			")\r",
			"print(resp[\"choices\"][0][\"message\"][\"content\"])\r",
			"\r",
			"# Streaming\r",
			"for chunk in llm(\"Explain quantum computing:\", max_tokens=256, stream=True):\r",
			"    print(chunk[\"choices\"][0][\"text\"], end=\"\", flush=True)\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Embeddings\r",
			"\r",
			"```python\r",
			"llm = Llama(model_path=\"./model-q4_k_m.gguf\", embedding=True, n_gpu_layers=35)\r",
			"vec = llm.embed(\"This is a test sentence.\")\r",
			"print(f\"Embedding dimension: {len(vec)}\")\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"You can also load a GGUF straight from the Hub:\r",
			"\r",
			"```python\r",
			"llm = Llama.from_pretrained(\r",
			"    repo_id=\"bartowski/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-GGUF\",\r",
			"    filename=\"*Q4_K_M.gguf\",\r",
			"    n_gpu_layers=35,\r",
			")\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"## Choosing a quant\r",
			"\r",
			"Use the Hub page first, generic heuristics second.\r",
			"\r",
			"- Prefer the exact quant that HF marks as compatible for the user's hardware profile.\r",
			"- For general chat, start with `Q4_K_M`.\r",
			"- For code or technical work, prefer `Q5_K_M` or `Q6_K` if memory allows.\r",
			"- For very tight RAM budgets, consider `Q3_K_M`, `IQ` variants, or `Q2` variants only if the user explicitly prioritizes fit over quality.\r",
			"- For multimodal repos, mention `mmproj-*.gguf` separately. The projector is not the main model file.\r",
			"- Do not normalize repo-native labels. If the page says `UD-Q4_K_M`, report `UD-Q4_K_M`.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Extracting available GGUFs from a repo\r",
			"\r",
			"When the user asks what GGUFs exist, return:\r",
			"\r",
			"- filename\r",
			"- file size\r",
			"- quant label\r",
			"- whether it is a main model or an auxiliary projector\r",
			"\r",
			"Ignore unless requested:\r",
			"\r",
			"- README\r",
			"- BF16 shard files\r",
			"- imatrix blobs or calibration artifacts\r",
			"\r",
			"Use the tree API for this step:\r",
			"\r",
			"- `https://huggingface.co/api/models/<repo>/tree/main?recursive=true`\r",
			"\r",
			"For a repo like `unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF`, the local-app page can show quant chips such as `UD-Q4_K_M`, `UD-Q5_K_M`, `UD-Q6_K`, and `Q8_0`, while the tree API exposes exact file paths such as `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_M.gguf` and `Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Q8_0.gguf` with byte sizes. Use the tree API to turn a quant label into an exact filename.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Search patterns\r",
			"\r",
			"Use these URL shapes directly:\r",
			"\r",
			"```text\r",
			"https://huggingface.co/models?apps=llama.cpp&sort=trending\r",
			"https://huggingface.co/models?search=<term>&apps=llama.cpp&sort=trending\r",
			"https://huggingface.co/models?search=<term>&apps=llama.cpp&num_parameters=min:0,max:24B&sort=trending\r",
			"https://huggingface.co/<repo>?local-app=llama.cpp\r",
			"https://huggingface.co/api/models/<repo>/tree/main?recursive=true\r",
			"https://huggingface.co/<repo>/tree/main\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"## Output format\r",
			"\r",
			"When answering discovery requests, prefer a compact structured result like:\r",
			"\r",
			"```text\r",
			"Repo: <repo>\r",
			"Recommended quant from HF: <label> (<size>)\r",
			"llama-server: <command>\r",
			"Other GGUFs:\r",
			"- <filename> - <size>\r",
			"- <filename> - <size>\r",
			"Source URLs:\r",
			"- <local-app URL>\r",
			"- <tree API URL>\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"## References\r",
			"\r",
			"- **[hub-discovery.md](references/hub-discovery.md)** - URL-only Hugging Face workflows, search patterns, GGUF extraction, and command reconstruction\r",
			"- **[advanced-usage.md](references/advanced-usage.md)** — speculative decoding, batched inference, grammar-constrained generation, LoRA, multi-GPU, custom builds, benchmark scripts\r",
