			"| Experimental auto-detection       | `informed`         | Auto-detects alignment type — experimental, may not always outperform advanced |\r",
			"\r",
			"### 9 CLI Methods\r",
			"- **basic** — Single refusal direction via diff-in-means. Fast (~5-10 min for 8B).\r",
			"- **advanced** (DEFAULT, RECOMMENDED) — Multiple SVD directions, norm-preserving projection, 2 refinement passes. Medium speed (~10-20 min).\r",
			"- **aggressive** — Whitened SVD + jailbreak-contrastive + attention head surgery. Higher risk of coherence damage.\r",
			"- **spectral_cascade** — DCT frequency-domain decomposition. Research/novel approach.\r",
			"- **informed** — Runs analysis DURING abliteration to auto-configure. Experimental — slower and less predictable than advanced.\r",
			"- **surgical** — SAE features + neuron masking + head surgery + per-expert. Very slow (~1-2 hrs). Best for reasoning models.\r",
			"- **optimized** — Bayesian hyperparameter search (Optuna TPE). Longest runtime but finds optimal parameters.\r",
			"- **inverted** — Flips the refusal direction. Model becomes actively willing.\r",
			"- **nuclear** — Maximum force combo for stubborn MoE models. Expert-granular.\r",
			"\r",
			"### Direction Extraction Methods (--direction-method flag)\r",
			"- **diff_means** (default) — Simple difference-in-means between refused/complied activations. Robust.\r",
			"- **svd** — Multi-direction SVD extraction. Better for complex alignment.\r",
			"- **leace** — LEACE (Linear Erasure via Closed-form Estimation). Optimal linear erasure.\r",
			"\r",
