			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\r",
			"    \"query\": \"mutation($input: ProjectCreateInput!) { projectCreate(input: $input) { success project { id name url } } }\",\r",
			"    \"variables\": {\r",
			"      \"input\": {\r",
			"        \"name\": \"Q2 Auth Overhaul\",\r",
			"        \"description\": \"Replace legacy auth with OAuth2 and PKCE\",\r",
			"        \"teamIds\": [\"TEAM_UUID\"]\r",
			"      }\r",
			"    }\r",
			"  }' | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"## Documents\r",
			"\r",
			"Linear **Documents** are prose docs (RFCs, specs, notes) stored alongside issues. They have their own `documents` root query and `document(id:)` single-fetch.\r",
			"\r",
			"### Document URLs and `slugId`\r",
			"\r",
			"Document URLs look like:\r",
			"```\r",
			"https://linear.app/<workspace>/document/<slug>-<hexSlugId>\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"The trailing hex segment is the `slugId`. Example: `https://linear.app/nousresearch/document/rfc-hermes-permission-gateway-discord-38359beef67c` → `slugId` is `38359beef67c`.\r",
			"\r",
			"**Important schema detail:** the Markdown body is in the `content` field. The ProseMirror JSON is in `contentState` (not `contentData` — that field does not exist and the API returns 400).\r",
			"\r",
			"### Fetch a document by slugId\r",
			"\r",
			"`document(id:)` only accepts UUIDs. To fetch by the URL's hex slug, filter the collection:\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \\\r",
			"  -H \"Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY\" \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\"query\": \"query($s: String!) { documents(filter: { slugId: { eq: $s } }, first: 1) { nodes { id title content contentState slugId url creator { name } project { name } updatedAt } } }\", \"variables\": {\"s\": \"38359beef67c\"}}' \\\r",
			"  | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Or via the Python helper:\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"python3 scripts/linear_api.py get-document 38359beef67c\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Fetch a document by UUID\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \\\r",
			"  -H \"Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY\" \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\"query\": \"{ document(id: \\\"11700cff-b514-4db3-afcc-3ed1afacba1c\\\") { title content url } }\"}' \\\r",
			"  | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### List recent documents\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \\\r",
			"  -H \"Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY\" \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\"query\": \"{ documents(first: 25, orderBy: updatedAt) { nodes { id title slugId url updatedAt project { name } } } }\"}' \\\r",
			"  | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Search documents by title\r",
			"\r",
			"Linear's schema has no `searchDocuments` root. Use a title-substring filter instead:\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \\\r",
			"  -H \"Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY\" \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\"query\": \"{ documents(filter: { title: { containsIgnoreCase: \\\"RFC\\\" } }, first: 25) { nodes { title slugId url } } }\"}' \\\r",
			"  | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"## Pagination\r",
			"\r",
			"Linear uses Relay-style cursor pagination:\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"# First page\r",
			"curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \\\r",
			"  -H \"Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY\" \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\"query\": \"{ issues(first: 20) { nodes { identifier title } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } }\"}' | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"\r",
			"# Next page — use endCursor from previous response\r",
			"curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \\\r",
			"  -H \"Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY\" \\\r",
			"  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r",
			"  -d '{\"query\": \"{ issues(first: 20, after: \\\"CURSOR_FROM_PREVIOUS\\\") { nodes { identifier title } pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor } } }\"}' | python3 -m json.tool\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Default page size: 50. Max: 250. Always use `first: N` to limit results.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Filtering Reference\r",
			"\r",
			"Comparators: `eq`, `neq`, `in`, `nin`, `lt`, `lte`, `gt`, `gte`, `contains`, `startsWith`, `containsIgnoreCase`\r",
			"\r",
			"Combine filters with `or: [...]` for OR logic (default is AND within a filter object).\r",
			"\r",
			"## Typical Workflow\r",
			"\r",
			"1. **Query teams** to get team IDs and keys\r",
			"2. **Query workflow states** for target team to get state UUIDs\r",
			"3. **List or search issues** to find what needs work\r",
			"4. **Create issues** with team ID, title, description, priority\r",
			"5. **Update status** by setting `stateId` to the target workflow state\r",
			"6. **Add comments** to track progress\r",
			"7. **Mark complete** by setting `stateId` to the team's \"completed\" type state\r",
			"\r",
			"## Rate Limits\r",
			"\r",
