			"\r",
			"Returns bounding box coordinates, width/height in km, and approximate area.\r",
			"Useful as input for the bbox command.\r",
			"\r",
			"### bbox — Search within a bounding box\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"python3 $MAPS bbox 40.75 -74.00 40.77 -73.98 restaurant --limit 20\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Finds POIs within a geographic rectangle. Use `area` first to get the\r",
			"bounding box coordinates for a named place.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Working With Telegram Location Pins\r",
			"\r",
			"When a user sends a location pin, the message contains `latitude:` and\r",
			"`longitude:` fields. Extract those and pass them straight to `nearby`:\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"# User sent a pin at 36.17, -115.14 and asked \"find cafes nearby\"\r",
			"python3 $MAPS nearby 36.17 -115.14 cafe --radius 1500\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Present results as a numbered list with names, distances, and the\r",
			"`maps_url` field so the user gets a tap-to-open link in chat. For \"open\r",
			"now?\" questions, check the `hours` field; if missing or unclear, verify\r",
			"with `web_search` since OSM hours are community-maintained and not always\r",
			"current.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Workflow Examples\r",
			"\r",
			"**\"Find Italian restaurants near the Colosseum\":**\r",
			"1. `nearby --near \"Colosseum Rome\" --category restaurant --radius 500`\r",
			"   — one command, auto-geocoded\r",
			"\r",
			"**\"What's near this location pin they sent?\":**\r",
			"1. Extract lat/lon from the Telegram message\r",
			"2. `nearby LAT LON cafe --radius 1500`\r",
			"\r",
			"**\"How do I walk from hotel to conference center?\":**\r",
			"1. `directions \"Hotel Name\" --to \"Conference Center\" --mode walking`\r",
			"\r",
			"**\"What restaurants are in downtown Seattle?\":**\r",
			"1. `area \"Downtown Seattle\"` → get bounding box\r",
			"2. `bbox S W N E restaurant --limit 30`\r",
			"\r",
			"## Pitfalls\r",
			"\r",
			"- Nominatim ToS: max 1 req/s (handled automatically by the script)\r",
			"- `nearby` requires lat/lon OR `--near \"<address>\"` — one of the two is needed\r",
			"- OSRM routing coverage is best for Europe and North America\r",
			"- Overpass API can be slow during peak hours; the script automatically\r",
			"  falls back between mirrors (overpass-api.de → overpass.kumi.systems)\r",
			"- `distance` and `directions` use `--to` flag for the destination (not positional)\r",
			"- If a zip code alone gives ambiguous results globally, include country/state\r",
			"\r",
			"## Verification\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
