			"npm install --global ntn\r",
			"\r",
			"ntn --version    # verify\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"**Skip `ntn login` — use the integration token instead.** This works headlessly, no browser needed:\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"export NOTION_API_TOKEN=$NOTION_API_KEY      # ntn reads NOTION_API_TOKEN\r",
			"export NOTION_KEYRING=0                       # don't try to use the OS keychain\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Add those exports to your shell profile (or to `~/.hermes/.env`) so every session inherits them.\r",
			"\r",
			"### 3. Choose path at runtime\r",
			"\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"if command -v ntn >/dev/null 2>&1; then\r",
			"  # use ntn\r",
			"else\r",
			"  # fall back to curl\r",
			"fi\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Windows users: skip step 2 entirely until native `ntn` ships — Path B works fine. If you want CLI ergonomics now, install `ntn` inside WSL2.\r",
			"\r",
			"## API Basics\r",
			"\r",
			"`Notion-Version: 2025-09-03` is required on all HTTP requests. `ntn` handles this for you. In this version, what users call \"databases\" are called **data sources** in the API.\r",
			"\r",
			"## Path A — `ntn` CLI (preferred, macOS / Linux)\r",
			"\r",
			"### Raw API calls (shorthand for curl)\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"ntn api v1/users                                  # GET\r",
			"ntn api v1/pages parent[page_id]=abc123 \\         # POST with inline body\r",
			"  properties[title][0][text][content]=\"Notes\"\r",
			"ntn api v1/pages/abc123 -X PATCH archived:=true   # PATCH; := is non-string (bool/num/null)\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"Syntax notes:\r",
			"- `key=value` — string fields\r",
			"- `key[nested]=value` — nested object fields\r",
			"- `key:=value` — typed assignment (booleans, numbers, null, arrays)\r",
			"\r",
			"### Search\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"ntn api v1/search query=\"page title\"\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Read page metadata\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"ntn api v1/pages/{page_id}\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Read page as Markdown (agent-friendly)\r",
			"```bash\r",
			"ntn api v1/pages/{page_id}/markdown\r",
			"```\r",
			"\r",
			"### Read page content as blocks\r",
